# Figma (MVDS)

## MCP

Cursor: Figma plugin / MCP (`plugin-figma-figma`). Before `use_figma`, load the figma-use skill. MVDS-specific sync skills live under `.claude/skills/mvds-figma-*` — **run only when the founder explicitly asks** (AGENTS.md / docs/SYNC.md).

## Source of truth

**Code is law.** MVDS Core (`fileKey C20nU0mROzk3Zr0I9BELJF`) is a generated, one-way mirror (code → Figma). Scratch/prototype frames for OpenSpec iteration are allowed in `design.md`; do not treat Figma as upstream for tokens or component APIs.

## Map to MVDS — not hub kits

- Tokens: `src/index.css` / Tailwind `@theme` (`bg-background`, `text-h1`, 8-grid spacing, etc.)
- Layout: `Stack` / `Inline` / `Grid` / `Container` — never raw flex/grid utilities for page layout
- Components: `src/components/ui/`, `layout/`, `site/`, `blocks/`
- Treat Figma MCP export as **reference**; rewrite to MVDS primitives and tokens

## HF (High Fidelity) explorations bind the published MVDS Core library

Design-gate scratch files (the as-is + proposed pairs below) are **HF — "High
Fidelity" — artifacts** (founder naming, 2026-08-23), and an HF file **ingests
the system's scales instead of hand-mirroring them**:

1. Read variable names + keys from MVDS Core (`C20nU0mROzk3Zr0I9BELJF`):
   collections **Tokens** (Light/Dark), **Scales**, **Customize Here** —
   `getLocalVariableCollectionsAsync()` in the Core file, `variable.key` per
   variable.
2. In the scratch file, `figma.variables.importVariableByKeyAsync(key)` and
   bind fills / text / gaps to the imported variables. Dark boards flip via
   the collection's variable **mode** — never a second hand-painted set.
3. **Gotcha:** `teamLibrary.getAvailableLibraryVariableCollectionsAsync()`
   lists only libraries *enabled in that file's UI* and returns `[]` in fresh
   drafts. That does **not** mean MVDS Core is unpublished — import-by-key
   works regardless. Do not fall back to hand-mirrored hex on an empty
   listing.

Hand-mirrored values are the exception, not the default: allowed only for a
token Core doesn't carry yet (e.g. proposed-but-unshipped tokens), flagged as
reference in the frame and in design.md. If Core trails `src/index.css`, say
so in design.md's Libraries/version row — the fix is the founder-requested
token sync, not silent hex.

## Proposal file page naming (scratch / explore files)

When iterating UI in a Figma design file (not MVDS Core library sync), use **one page per step**. Never overwrite a prior page — create a new page for each proposal iteration.

| Page name | Role |
|---|---|
| `0.0 As is` | **First page.** Map the current product/surface faithfully (what ships today). No proposed IA. |
| `01.0 Propose: <openspec-change>` | First proposal for OpenSpec change `<openspec-change>` (kebab-case slug). |
| `02.0 Propose: <openspec-change> update` | Next iteration (then `03.0` …). Append ` update` (and bump the numeric prefix). |

Rules:

- Always create `0.0 As is` before any `Propose:` page.
- Page names carry the **OpenSpec change slug** after `Propose:` so design.md and Figma stay aligned.
- Leave prior pages untouched when direction changes — new page, new number.

## OpenSpec `design.md`

**The Figma gate is not skippable.** Every change that adds or alters UI MUST produce an **as-is + proposed pair** before `design.md` is approved — not a table promising one later:

1. **`0.0 As is`** — the current surface reconstructed from code (or captured from a running Storybook story). Flag non-code-derivable values as reference.
2. **`0N.0 Propose: <change-slug>`** — the changed surface on MVDS tokens and layout primitives. New numbered page per iteration.

Then the **Visual design / Figma** table records:

- Primary Figma file URL (MVDS Core and/or scratch)
- **As-is page / frame** and **proposed page / frame**, by name
- Libraries **and version** (MVDS Core Tokens/Scales/components; key or `@beckharrisdesign/mvds@x.y.z`)
- Breakpoints (S=480 / L=1024 unless Storybook-only)
- Status (draft / iterating / ready for apply)

**"Reuses existing components" is not grounds to skip.** Reused components still get placed in a proposed frame — that IS the design review.

**Removals count as UI changes.** Deleting a variant, prop, export, story, or visible component gets the same pair; the proposed page shows the surface with the element absent (e.g. the button row with one fewer variant). "There's nothing to design" is not grounds to skip (hub precedent: `remove-workflow-page`, 2026-07-21). MVDS is pre-1.0 and removes rather than deprecates (AGENTS.md), so removals are a routine case here.

**N/A is allowed ONLY for genuinely API-only / no-UI changes** — one "N/A — no UI" row with rationale. If the change renders anything a user sees, it is not API-only.

## Stage model (mvds-default schema)

Under the default `mvds-default` schema this design gate sits inside a stage
model (openspec: adding-eval-gate): **0.5 Eval**, **0.6 Eval Summary**, and
**1.5 Eval Delta**. The **canonical** stage artifacts are markdown in the
change directory (`discovery.md` / `design.md`) — that is what conditions
generation and what the delta dispositions against. But the number line is
the page order, so every stage **also lands as a page** in the HF file
(founder amendment, 2026-08-26 — an eval you can only read outside Figma
doesn't review like one):

| Page | Stage | Content |
|---|---|---|
| `0.0 As is` | discovery | the current surface, faithfully |
| `0.5 Eval` | discovery | duplicates of the as-is frames pinned with numbered findings (F1…), plus per-rubric summary and 0.6 Eval Summary boards |
| `0N.0 Propose: <change>` | design | proposed surface, conditioned on the approved 0.6 |
| `0N.5 Eval Delta` | design | duplicates of that iteration's propose frames pinned with the disposition of every baseline finding (addressed / preserved / regressed / new) |

Pins and boards are an **annotation layer** — hand-styled chrome is fine
there; the surface frames they sit on keep their variable bindings. Markdown
stays canonical: don't hand-edit page annotations without updating the
markdown, and never treat the pages as the source the next stage generates
from. The running Storybook story is still the eval *target* where one
exists; the pages are the visual record.

## Code Connect

MVDS does **not** use Code Connect (AGENTS.md). Do not add `.figma.ts` connect files unless the founder changes that policy.
